The tidyverse is a collection of packages built for data science. It is more readable, consistent syntax across packages

```{r tidyverse}
library(tidyverse)
```


### 1. tidyverse & tibbles

```{r tibble()}
df <- read.csv('gapminder.csv')
df <- as_tibble(df)
head(df, 3)
```

### 2. dplyr: Core Verbs

select()
```{r select()}
df |> select(country, year, gdpPercap)
df |> select(-continent)
```

filter()
```{r filter()}
df |> filter(year == 2007)
df |> filter(continent == 'Asia' & year == 2007)
```

mutate()
```{r mutate()}
df |> 
  mutate(
    gdp = gdpPercap + pop,
    lifeExp = round(lifeExp),
    gdp_updated = gdp * 1.02
  )
```

arrange()
```{r arrange()}
df |> arrange(desc(lifeExp))
```

summarize()
```{r summarize()}
df |> summarize(pop_mean = mean(pop), 
                pop_med = median(pop))
```

group_by()
```{r group_by()}
df |> 
  filter(year == 2007) |>
  group_by(continent) |> 
  summarize(mean_life = mean(lifeExp), num = n())
```

dplyr Verb Summary
```{r dplyr summary}
df |>
  filter(year == 2007) |>              # 1. reduce rows first
  select(-gdpPercap) |>                # 2. drop unneeded columns
  mutate(lifeExp = round(lifeExp)) |>  # 3. transform before grouping
  group_by(continent) |>               # 4. group, if needed
  summarize(avg_le = mean(lifeExp)) |> # 5. collapse to one row per group
  arrange(desc(abg_le)) |>             # 6. sort once data is ready
  head()                               # 7. trim to final rows last
```

### 3. tidyr: Reshaping Data

```{r pivoting before}
df_before <- tibble(
  country = c("Afghanistan", "Afghanistan", "Afghanistan", "Albania", "Albania", "Albania"),
  year    = c(1997, 2002, 2007, 1997, 2002, 2007),
  lifeExp = c(41.8, 42.1, 43.8, 72.9, 75.6, 76.4)
)
df_before
```

```{r pivoting after}
df_after = df_before |> pivot_wider(names_from = year, values_from = lifeExp)
df_after
```

### 4. lubridate: working with dates
```{r}
dates <- c("2026-09-14", "2026-09-15",
           "2026-09-16", "2026-09-17",
           "2026-09-18", "2026-09-19")
day(ymd(dates))
```

### 5. tidyverse Review
dplyr — manipulate data
tidyr — reshape/tidy data
lubridate — work with dates and times
tibble — the modern dataframe format
readr — read data in and write to files
ggplot2 — visualize data






